# DevGuard Environment Configuration
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to '.env' if using the AI commit-message feature:
#    cp .env.example .env
# 2. Configure your preferred AI provider below.
# 3. NEVER commit your actual '.env' file or keys to version control.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ── AI Provider selection ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Choose which AI provider DevGuard uses. Options: gemini | ollama
# If not set, DevGuard auto-detects: prefers Gemini when GEMINI_API_KEY is
# present, falls back to Ollama when OLLAMA_* vars are present.
# DEVGUARD_AI_PROVIDER=gemini

# ── Google Gemini ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required only when DEVGUARD_AI_PROVIDER=gemini (or auto-detected as Gemini).
# Install the SDK: pip install 'devguard[ai]'
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Gemini model to use. Defaults to gemini-2.5-flash.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# ── Ollama (local, no API key needed) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Required only when DEVGUARD_AI_PROVIDER=ollama (or auto-detected as Ollama).
# Ollama uses only stdlib — no extra pip packages needed.
# Start the Ollama server first: ollama serve
#
# Base URL of the Ollama server. Defaults to http://localhost:11434.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
#
# Model tag to use. Pull it first: ollama pull llama3.2
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

